## Quantum Loop

I made Quantum Loop almost entirely solo, using a custom engine based on
the *PyGame* framework. It's my first commercial game, published on
*Steam* in November 2025. Leading up to release I was given the
opportunity to showcase at *PAX Aus*, *SXSW Sydney*, and *Steam Next
Fest*!

It's a non-linear adventure game in a time loop, all about
problem-solving by exploiting your knowledge of the world. With no quest
log or specific directions, there's a big emphasis on player choice and
freedom. Objectives can be completed in a multitude of ways that aren't
explicitly stated.

I started Quantum Loop in January 2024 as a passion project, and after
over a year and a half of development released it on Steam on 26
November 2025. I made almost everything, excluding the promotional art
and about half of the soundtrack, which a couple of my talented friends
helped with. I ran regular playtests and used everything I'd learnt
about iterative design, as the game concept slowly morphed from a simple
space-sim into the unique gameplay flow it has today.

Releasing Quantum Loop was one of the most incredible experiences I've
ever had. I learnt so much about managing large-scale game projects and
getting a game ready to ship, and I'm immensely proud of how it turned
out.

`Python / PyGame / Game Design / Sound Design / Music / Playtesting / Self-Publishing / Steamworks`

[Trailer](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GNcofO9motE) [Get it on
Steam!](https://store.steampowered.com/app/3186440/Quantum_Loop/)

