# Accessibility

my master's thesis was on practical game accessibility in the
mainstream.

## Game Accessibility Advice

I am available for consulting on your game's accessibility
considerations. I can give practical advice on many categories,
including subtitles, controls, colour blindness considerations, visual
clarity, and more.

As an independent developer myself, I know the practical difficulties
involved and can help identify simple ways to make your game playable by
as many people as possible. It can feel challenging to maintain your
game's vision while maximising access, and I aim to help with this,
widening the audience that gets to experience your game. If it suits
your project, I can also offer early design advice so that you can make
more fundamental decisions towards wider access.

My number one suggestion to anyone who wants to make their game more
accessible is to playtest it with people who have the needs you're
catering for. I can find basic issues and give your team direction, but
will always recommend a playtesting approach to solve issues more
deeply.

If you want my help making your game work for a wider audience, send me
an email!

[Get in touch](mailto:declancarveth@gmail.com)

